entity story                      # one story in a spec_file
  id                              # FUL-005
  file: one spec_file
  sentence
  role_name
  epic_id, optional
  text                            # the story as it stands in the file, every line
  rules_text                      # its operations and examples only, with comments,
                                  #   blank lines and trailing spaces removed
  approvals: many approval, in order    # oldest first; the newest is approvals[-1]
  version: count(approvals)
  is approved: count(approvals) is more than 0
    and rules_text is approvals[-1]'s rules_text
  may create: agent
  may read:   agent, operator
  may update: agent
  may delete: nobody

entity approval, part of story    # one block in the .edda.vc file
  version
  approved_at
  approved_by
  because, optional
  text                            # the whole story as approved
  rules_text                      # its operations and examples, normalised as above

story a story is a draft until the operator approves it     # EDDA-004
  as an operator
  i want a story whose operations or examples differ from its newest
    approved copy to be a draft, whoever changed it
  so that nothing the agent writes counts until I have said yes
  epic: VC
  tags: version, approval

  example a new story is a draft
    given story fresh with id "FUL-010", approvals []
    then  fresh is not approved

  example a story that matches its newest approval is approved
    given approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\""
          story same with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            rules_text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\""
    then  same is approved

  example a changed refusal makes a draft again
    given approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\""
          story changed with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            rules_text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"the order is already removed\""
    then  changed is not approved

  example a changed example makes a draft again
    given approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "example a\n  given order o with status incoming\n  then  o's status is incoming"
          story changed with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            rules_text "example a\n  given order o with status removed\n  then  o's status is removed"
    then  changed is not approved

  example a changed label, comment or blank line does not make a draft
    given approval a1 with version 1, text "story remove orders            # FUL-005\n  tags: shop\n  operation remove(order)\n    # frees the stock\n    when remove succeeds, ensure:\n      the order's status is removed",
            rules_text "operation remove(order)\n  when remove succeeds, ensure:\n    the order's status is removed"
          story relabelled with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            text "story remove orders            # FUL-005\n  tags: shop, ordering\n\n  operation remove(order)\n    # frees the held stock\n    when remove succeeds, ensure:\n      the order's status is removed  ",
            rules_text "operation remove(order)\n  when remove succeeds, ensure:\n    the order's status is removed"
    then  relabelled is approved

story the operator approves a story and the copy is kept    # EDDA-005
  as an operator
  i want my yes to append the whole story as the next version to the
    .edda.vc file, with the date, my name and one line of because
  so that every approved version is kept exactly, in order, and the
    agent cannot write it
  epic: VC
  tags: version, approval
  note: the agent is kept out of .edda.vc by a repository guard outside
    the language; that guard is level 2 and is tested there

  operation approve(story: story, because optional)
    who: operator
    if the story is approved,
      refuse: "nothing to approve: the story matches its newest version"
    if any(p's kind is refused for p in check(story's file)),
      refuse: "the file does not check"
    when approve succeeds, ensure:
      story's approvals is the old story's approvals + [story's approvals[-1]]
      story's approvals[-1]'s version is the old story's version + 1
      story's approvals[-1]'s text is story's text
      story's approvals[-1]'s rules_text is story's rules_text
      story's approvals[-1]'s approved_by is the actor
      story's approvals[-1]'s approved_at is now
      story's approvals[-1]'s because is because
      the story is approved

  example the first approval makes version 1
    given operator tuan
          spec_file good from fixture order
    when  tuan asks approve(good's stories[0], "the shop asked for it") at 2026-10-02 09:00
    then  done
          good's stories[0]'s version is 1
          good's stories[0]'s approvals[0]'s approved_by is tuan
          good's stories[0]'s approvals[0]'s approved_at is 2026-10-02 09:00
          good's stories[0]'s approvals[0]'s because is "the shop asked for it"
          good's stories[0] is approved

  example a second approval keeps the first and adds version 2
    given operator tuan
          approval a1 with version 1, approved_at 2026-10-01 14:00, rules_text "R1", text "T1"
          story grown with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1], rules_text "R2", text "T2", file good
          spec_file good from fixture order
    when  tuan asks approve(grown) at 2026-10-02 09:00
    then  done
          grown's version is 2
          grown's approvals[0] is a1
          grown's approvals[1]'s version is 2
          grown's approvals[1]'s rules_text is "R2"
          grown's approvals[1]'s because is empty
          grown is approved

  example approving an approved story is refused
    given operator tuan
          approval a1 with version 1, rules_text "R1"
          story same with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1], rules_text "R1", file good
          spec_file good from fixture order
    when  tuan asks approve(same)
    then  refused: "nothing to approve: the story matches its newest version"
          same's version is 1

  example a story in a file that does not check is refused
    given operator tuan
          spec_file bad from fixture unknown_keyword
    when  tuan asks approve(bad's stories[0])
    then  refused: "the file does not check"
          bad's stories[0]'s version is 0

  example the agent may not approve
    given agent bot
          spec_file good from fixture order
    when  bot asks approve(good's stories[0])
    then  refused: "agent may not approve"
          good's stories[0]'s version is 0

story the operator sees what changed before saying yes      # EDDA-006
  as an operator
  i want the difference between the story in the file and its newest
    approved copy as added and removed lines, in order
  so that I read the change, not the whole story, every time
  epic: VC
  tags: version, diff

  operation diff(story: story) returns story's changes
    who: agent, operator
    note: a line of the story, with its indentation and without its
      comment, is a sentence; a sentence is removed when it is in the
      newest approved text and not in the story's text, added when the
      other way round; the same sentence twice counts twice; changes are
      ordered by line

  example an added refusal shows as added
    given approval a1 with version 1, text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\""
          story grown with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\"\n  if the order's units_sent is more than 0,\n    refuse: \"already sent\""
    when  operator asks diff(grown) as d
    then  done
          count(d) is 2
          d[0]'s kind is added
          d[0]'s line is 4
          d[0]'s sentence is "  if the order's units_sent is more than 0,"
          d[1]'s kind is added
          d[1]'s sentence is "    refuse: \"already sent\""

  example a changed reason shows as one removed and one added
    given approval a1 with version 1, text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"already removed\""
          story reworded with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            text "operation remove(order)\n  if the order's status is removed,\n    refuse: \"the order is already removed\""
    when  operator asks diff(reworded) as d
    then  done
          count(d) is 2
          d[0]'s kind is removed
          d[0]'s sentence is "    refuse: \"already removed\""
          d[1]'s kind is added
          d[1]'s sentence is "    refuse: \"the order is already removed\""

  example a comment-only edit shows nothing
    given approval a1 with version 1, text "operation remove(order)   # frees stock\n  when remove succeeds, ensure:\n    the order's status is removed"
          story commented with id "FUL-005", approvals [a1],
            text "operation remove(order)   # frees the held stock\n  when remove succeeds, ensure:\n    the order's status is removed"
    when  operator asks diff(commented) as d
    then  done
          d is []

  example a story never approved shows every line as added
    given story fresh with id "FUL-010", approvals [],
            text "operation remove(order)\n  when remove succeeds, ensure:\n    the order's status is removed"
    when  operator asks diff(fresh) as d
    then  done
          count(d) is 3
          all(c's kind is added for c in d)

story the operator reads a story as sentences               # EDDA-007
  as an operator
  i want a story shown as plain sentences in its own order, one per
    rule, with the ids hidden and the notes in grey
  so that I read the business meaning, never the syntax
  epic: VIEW
  tags: read-view

  operation view(story: story) returns story's sentences
    who: agent, operator
    note: a name reads as words: units_sent reads "units sent"

  operation view_at(story: story, version) returns
    the sentences of story's approvals[version - 1]'s text
    who: agent, operator
    if version is more than story's version,
      refuse: "no such version"

  example the clean fixture reads as six sentences
    given spec_file good from fixture order
    when  operator asks view(good's stories[0]) as v
    then  done
          count(v) is 6
          v[0]'s kind is story
          v[0]'s text is "Remove an order. As a shop user, I want to remove an order, so that the list is clean."
          v[1]'s kind is permission
          v[1]'s text is "A shop user may remove an order."
          v[2]'s kind is refusal
          v[2]'s text is "IF the order's units sent is more than 0, THEN refuse: already sent."
          v[3]'s kind is outcome
          v[3]'s text is "WHEN remove succeeds, the order's status SHALL be removed."
          v[4]'s kind is example
          v[4]'s text is "Example: a fresh order is removed."
          v[5]'s kind is example
          v[5]'s text is "Given a shop user erik and an order purchase with status incoming and units sent 0, when erik asks to remove purchase, then it is done and purchase's status is removed."

  example a note reads in its place and a question after it
    given spec_file a from fixture notes_a
    when  operator asks view(a's stories[0]) as v
    then  done
          v[1]'s kind is note
          v[1]'s text is "the stock feed is refreshed every night"

  example no sentence shows an id
    given spec_file good from fixture order
    when  operator asks view(good's stories[0]) as v
    then  done
          not any("FIX-001" in s's text for s in v)

  example an older version reads from its approved copy
    given approval a1 with version 1, text "story remove an order   # FIX-001\n  as a shop_user\n  i want to remove an order\n  so that the list is clean\n  operation remove(order: order)\n    when remove succeeds, ensure:\n      the order's status is removed"
          story grown with id "FIX-001", approvals [a1],
            text "story remove an order   # FIX-001\n  as a shop_user\n  i want to remove an order\n  so that the list is clean\n  operation remove(order: order)\n    if the order's units_sent is more than 0,\n      refuse: \"already sent\"\n    when remove succeeds, ensure:\n      the order's status is removed"
    when  operator asks view_at(grown, 1) as v
    then  done
          not any(s's kind is refusal for s in v)
